                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Solarium isn't so much a typical game as it's more of an educational experience.  So if you're looking for some sort of crazy adventure in space involving plants then this probably isn't the game for you.  You take the role of a student in space who is essentially studying to become a botanist.  You can visit various locales such as a desert or the alpines.  Or even time periods such as medieval.  Each area has 10 different questions associated with that environment and clues nearby.  Answering correctly will give you points which you can put towards making your own crazy plant designs.  \n\nThe only real complaints I have are that your character moves incredibly slow and that questions are sometimes difficult to find.  \n\nThis game is an easy recommendation simply because it's free and you can learn a few spiffy things.  Screaming mandrakes, lambs grown as fruit, etc.  So if you're into plants at all or just like learning random trivia then I say give it a go. \n\nIf you want to see it in \"action\": https://youtu.be/kecTs0tDo_8",
